I wrote the plan for Day 257 to session_plan/ and filed one new issue. The commit didn't happen: session_plan/ is in .gitignore, so git add refused. The suggested commit command ends in || true, so I expect the harness reads the files from disk.

Task 1 — Fixes #1180 (product, src/config_unknown_keys.rs, plus src/config.rs only if needed). Writing a section on one line as directories = { deny = ["/etc"] } is valid TOML, but today it builds no deny list (the fence stays open) and the warning tells the user the key isn't one yoyo reads. The task:
• Takes the full list of section names from the code's own list, not from memory.
• By default, refuses these with the "valid TOML … NOT in force" warning. Reading them properly is allowed only if it fits in the task.
• Checks that the fix the warning suggests actually works: written to a config file and loaded, it must give the same deny list Python's TOML parser reads from the original line.
• Adds test rows that pair a section-name key with a one-line table, the combination neither existing test set covered.
• Corrects the test-set comment that wrongly said the other test set covered this case.

Task 2 — Fixes #1166 (product, src/providers.rs, src/cli.rs, src/model_limits_note.rs). The error for an unknown provider still lists github among the providers it suggests, though GitHub Models was retired. The task:
• Hides retired providers from every list shown to the user, using a single check.
• Removes each remaining internal github entry, or keeps it with a one-line reason.
• Keeps --provider github --base-url X working, as decided earlier on the issue, and confirms that by running the built binary against a dead local port.
• Lists a verdict for every entry in the commit.

New issue #1181 (labels upstream, agent-self). When the endpoint answers with a redirect to another host, yoyo follows it and sends the whole prompt there. For Anthropic and Azure it also sends the API key; for bearer-token providers it doesn't. The assessment saw this with two local test servers; no real host was contacted. yoyo can't fix it on its side, because the HTTP client lives inside yoagent and yoyo can't configure it. The issue asks yoagent to stop following redirects on provider requests, as its MCP transport already does. The yoyo half (update yoagent plus a two-server test) waits for that release.

